<article class="env-definition" id="007M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/007M">Definition <span data-tag="007M">6.15.1</span>.</a> A <em>type of algebraic structure</em> is given by a category $\mathcal{C}$ and a functor $F : \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ with the following properties </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$F$ is faithful, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{C}$ has limits and $F$ commutes with limits, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{C}$ has filtered colimits and $F$ commutes with them, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$F$ reflects isomorphisms. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>